#X obj 60 40 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty eps.i~\ and\ eps~ 24 6 0 22 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 60 76 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Ensoniq\ EPS\ /\ EPS-16\ PLUS\ /\ ASR-10\ instruments 24 6 0 16 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 60 120 eps.i~ 1;
#X text 190 120 <- click it: the editor, f 64;
#X obj 60 160 dac~;
#X obj 60 206 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty eps.i~ 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 234 eps.i~ is the whole instrument in one object: eps~ \, the editor \, the Launchkey surface (encoders \, pads and display \, see Launchkey) \, MIDI in and out. Put it in a patch \, put your Ensoniq instruments into a folder eps beside the patch \, connect the two left outlets to dac~ and play. Click it to open the editor \, see Editor. \; Argument 1 is the MIDI channel (0 or none = 1) \, argument 2 the channel of the pads (0 or none = 10 \, the Drums Channel) \, argument 3 the library folder (relative to the patch's folder or ~/... \, e.g. [eps.i~ 1 10 ~/Documents/Pd/eps-library]). Several eps.i~ do not get in each other's way \, each has its own editor and plays its own instrument. \; eps.i~ samples Pd's audio input 1 (input in the SAMPLE band: none \, 1 \, 2 or both) and whatever comes into its inlet 2: record new wavesamples with the SAMPLE band of the editor \, see Sampling. \; eps~ is the bare engine inside \, for patches of your own: inlet 2 takes the velocity of a note sent as a float \, inlet 3 raw MIDI bytes from midiin \, inlet 4 the audio to sample \, and the floats of outlet 3 (MIDI thru) go to midiout. eps~ alone takes the library beside the external \, or the folder given with library. Open eps.i~ to see the wiring., f 64;
#X obj 60 600 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Editor 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 628 The editor is the window of eps.i~. Every change shows up in it \, from the controller \, an instrument change or messages. refresh asks for all values again. \; Rows of 8 below the PATCH band \, titled as in Controls: row k is page k of the controller layer. Each cell: name and label \, a slider and a number box with the value as from a pot (0 to 127) \, the box beside it the value itself. \; PATCH band. name: the instrument that plays. library N: load instrument N of the whole library. reload: the instrument again \, edits dropped. init: all controls back to 0 \, the instrument stays. rescan: read the library folder again after adding files. \; folder: where you are \, as on the EPS: library is the top (disk images and EFE files) \, an image and its directories below (DISK1.img/BASSES). up: one folder up. file: the selected file with the arrows before and after it \, a directory ends in a slash. open: enter the directory or load the instrument. Loading an instrument shows its folder. \; Saving always writes the Ensoniq format \, so the EPS reads it. The offsets of the controls (cutoff \, attack ...) go into the instrument first and are set back to 0. replace: over the file the instrument was loaded from. save copy: a new file in the folder shown \, named after the instrument with a number. new name and save as: a new file of that name in the folder shown (in an image \, or an EFE at the top). new folder: a directory of that name \, inside an image. Names: up to 12 characters \, A-Z 0-9 space * - + (what the EPS lets you type) \, underscore for a space. See Library and saving. \; MIDI in: the receive channel \, 0 = all. out: the channel of the controller feedback. thru: see Messages \, thru. size: files in the folder \, library size: instruments in all. \; instrument: the locations 1-8 \, as the INSTRUMENT buttons of the EPS. Each holds an instrument and plays on its own MIDI channel (its MIDI ch \, location k on channel k at the start \, 0 = only when selected) \, the selected one also plays on MIDI in (the keys). Loading \, editing \, sampling \, saving and the controls act on the selected one. All share the one effect (FX=INST: the selected instrument's). delete instrument: the location empty. save bank: the locations \, their volumes and the bank effect as a bank file into the folder shown of a disk image (the instruments must be on that disk). A bank in the folder list loads with open: all locations emptied \, the bank's instruments into theirs \, the bank effect (FX=BANK). \; The other rows edit the loaded instrument itself (mouse only \, see Instrument rows). SELECT band: the layer and the wavesample the LAYER and WS rows show \, with their names and the key range \, root key \, rate and length of the wavesample. envelope: which one the ENV rows show (1 pitch \, 2 filter \, 3 amp). follow key (on by default): a played key selects its layer and wavesample \, the rows jump to their values \, and when several layers play the key \, the layer chosen stays and its wavesample follows. zero crossings (on by default): sample and loop points move to the nearest rising zero crossing. \; SAMPLE band: the wave recorder \, see Sampling. rate with its arrows \, threshold \, pre ms \, input (Pd's audio input: none \, 1 \, 2 \, 1+2) \, into (new WS \, replace WS \, new layer \, new instrument) \, level: the level display (the bars and the star of the threshold) \, rec and stop \, then the state and what it says. root key \, low key \, high key: the next key you play sets it for the selected wavesample. monitor: hear the input \, on or off whatever the recorder does (off by default \, with a microphone it feeds back). \; COMMAND band: the wavesample commands of the EPS for the selected wavesample \, see Wavesample commands. command with its arrows \, range (sample \, loop \, start to loop \, loop to end) \, do \, then old and new to compare \, keep or cancel. depth \, zone % \, scale % (start and end) \, rate \, smooth \, copy to layer and with data are the values the commands take. \; Sample and loop points have two cells each: the first sets the position coarsely \, in steps of 1/127 of the sample \, the second (fine) moves it by -64 to +63 samples from there. Loop pos moves loop start and end together \, the loop keeps its length (and pitch) \, as LOOPPOS on the EPS \, and shows the loop start. The box shows the sample number. Edits change the playing instrument at once (the next note \, filter \, amp \, pan \, LFO and wave modulation also sounding notes). They are kept with replace \, save copy or save as \, a reload or an instrument change drops them., f 64;
#X obj 60 1890 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Launchkey 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1918 eps~ drives the Launchkey Mini MK4 itself (custom firmware \, pads in Drum mode): the encoders \, the pads and the display follow two layers \, PLAY and EDIT. The pads have fixed meanings \, the display shows what they do. The bottom right pad 51 is MODE in both layers: pressed \, it switches PLAY and EDIT \, blue in PLAY \, purple in EDIT. On the switch the display shows the pads for 1.5 s. \; PLAY pads \, as on the EPS: the browser starts at the top level (the library \, the images as folders). 36 > and 44 < (cyan) go through the folder shown \, nothing loads. 42 OPEN (green \, bright on a folder): a folder: into it \, a patch: load it. 50 EXIT (yellow): one level up. After each step the display shows where you are (the folder \, what is selected). Also: 38 INIT (twice) \, 39 PAT> 47 PAT< (patch select \, pink) \, 41 SMPL (red) \, 46 SAVE (SAVE TO?: go to the folder with > < OPEN EXIT \, SAVE again: a copy with a free name there \, another pad: no) \, 48 SEL (held + OPEN: DELETE? the entry shown \, SEL: yes \, another pad: no \, a folder only when empty) \, 51 MODE. SEL held + a key C to G (any octave): select instrument location 1-8. SEL + SAVE: SAVE BANK TO? (the same \, then the bank). OPEN on a bank loads it. The encoders: CC page 1 of the Launchkey is P1 PERFORM \, page 2 is P2 PLAY (the same CC numbers as the controller layer of the Bela). \; EDIT pads \, top row: the areas INST LAYER WAVE PITCH FILTER AMP LFO ENV (pressed again: the next page of the area) \, each in its own colour: white \, yellow \, cyan \, pink \, lime \, amber \, sky \, magenta \, bright while its page is shown. Bottom row: 44 SEL (held: LAY> WS> ENV# step backwards \, a key selects its layer and wavesample without sound) \, 45 LAY> (next layer) \, 46 WS> (next wavesample of the layer) \, 47 ENV# (ENV1 > ENV2 > ENV3) \, 48 O/N \, 49 CMD \, 50 SMPL \, 51 MODE. The keys play \, follow key selects. The encoders act on the page shown \, whatever CC page the Launchkey is on: encoder n is cell n. \; The effect: INST pressed again shows E20 EFFECT \, the effect's parameters eight at a time \, named by the effect loaded (the display: effect name and page \, the encoders in four letters \, CH WET LEV 2 = CWL2). INST again: the next eight \, after the last E1 INST. On E20 O/N steps FX= OFF INST BANK ROM 1-13 (the display: mode \, name \, rate). SEL + O/N: LOAD EFFECT \, an effect file (SEL + O/N again: the next) \, O/N (flashing) loads it into the bank effect \, another pad: no. CMD: COPY TO BANK? (SEL + CMD: COPY TO INST? \, SAVE BANK EFFECT? \, DELETE INST EFFECT?) \, CMD again: do it \, another pad: no. VAR is the first encoder. The values as the EPS shows them. \; SMPL: the SAMPLE page E18 and the level display \, pressed again: record (from the threshold) \, again: stop \, then play the root key. CMD: the COMMAND page E19 \, the command chosen with encoder 1 \, pressed twice: run it. Then O/N plays the old or the new version (orange / green) \, CMD (now green) keeps the new one \, anything else keeps what plays. \; The display: one small line (page \, layer \, wavesample) \, then two big lines of 10 \, the chosen option underlined \, or a picture (envelope \, filters \, LFO). After a page change it shows the names of the 8 encoders. The values of the page go back to the encoders as CC (the firmware takes them). Pad colours: white = chosen \, dimmed = there \, dark = no function \, red = sampling (flashing while recording) \, orange = old \, green = new. \; The pages \, encoders 1 to 8 ((-) = not there yet): P1 PERFORM: CUT CUT2 FATT FDEC FREL AATT ADEC AREL | P2 PLAY: VOL TRNS WAVE FENV FX | E1 INST: TRNS KLO KHI PRES PMOD PROG MOUT XCTL | E2 LAYER: VLO VHI GLMD GLTM DLY DVEL RSTK LEG | E3 PATCHES: IN00 IN0* IN*0 IN** KYUP STLK PTBL | E4 WAVE: STRT STF END ENF LSTR LSF LEND LEF | E5 LOOP: LOOP LPOS LPF ALF KLO KHI | E6 WAVE MOD: WMSR WMAM WMTY WMRG | E7 PITCH: ROOT FINE BEND PENV PLFO PSRC PAMT RAND | E8 PITCH TBL: TBL(-) KEY(-) SEMI(-) FINE(-) | E9 FILTER: MODE CUT1 KEY1 ENV1 CUT2 KEY2 ENV2 | E10 FILT MOD: SRC1 AMT1 SRC2 AMT2 | E11 AMP: VOL PAN BOOS ASRC AAMT PNSR PNAM BUS | E12 XFADE: XFA XFB XFC XFD XFON | E13 LFO: WAVE SPD DPTH DLY MODE RSRC RAMT RNDF | E14 LFO DEPTH: DSRC DAMT | E15 ENV: T1 T2 T3 T4 L1 L2 L3 L4 | E16 RELEASE: T5 T6 L0 L5 MODE TYPE PSTE COPY | E17 SOFT: L0S L1S L2S L3S L4S T1V KBS VSW | E18 SAMPLE: RATE THRS PRE IN DEST MON | E19 COMMAND: CMD RNG DPTH ZONE SCL1 SCL2 RATE OPT | E20 EFFECT: FX1 FX2 FX3 FX4 FX5 FX6 FX7 FX8. \; The bare eps~ has the surface off (lk 1 switches it on). epscc and epspads \, the controller layer and the pads of the other instruments \, stay for patches of your own and the Bela., f 64;
#X obj 60 3180 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlet 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3208 eps.i~ 2 \, eps~ 4 signal: the audio to sample. \; 1 float: note number \, velocity 100. \; 1 list: note \, velocity and \, if you like \, the MIDI channel. \;   MIDI in eps.i~: notes \, bend \, pressure (channel and poly) \, \;   program change \, CC 1 wheel \, 2 XCTRL \, 4 pedal \, 7 volume \, \;   64 sustain. \; 1 anything: a message \, see Messages., f 64;
#X obj 60 3334 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3362 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: info \, name \, 0-127 and value text for every \;   change \, the instrument that plays \, its name \, the channels. \; 3 loaded model layers wavesamples: an instrument is in. \; 3 display title value: two lines for a display: a control \;   (Cutoff \, -12) \, the instrument (Preset 3 \, CLASSIC_PAD) \, \;   Loading \, saving (Saved \, PAD_BRIGHT). \; 3 folder text n \, bsel k n kind name: the folder shown \, \;   its size and the selected file (kind dir or inst). \; 3 saved: an instrument was written. \; 3 lkgfx bytes: a picture for the Launchkey display (envelope \, \;   filter \, LFO). lkgfx 0: off \, the text line stays. \; 3 recstate off / level / armed / recording / rootkey \, recinfo \;   text \, recmeter text (level display) \, recset rate / thresh / \;   pre / dest: the recorder. sampled ws layer: a recording is \;   in the instrument. \; 3 cmdstate idle / busy / new / old \, cmdinfo text \, cmdset \;   name value text: the wavesample commands., f 64;
#X obj 60 3680 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Library\ and\ saving 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3708 Where the library is: argument 3 of eps.i~ if there is one \, else the folder chosen with choose in the editor (kept in eps-library.txt beside the patch \, so it stays when the patch is opened again) \, else the folder eps beside the patch. Keep it apart from the folder with eps.i~ itself \, so an update of eps never touches it. \; The library holds Ensoniq disk images (IMG from a floppy \, HDA or IMG images of the hard disk on the SD card of a ZuluSCSI or BlueSCSI \, EDE \, EDA \, GKH) and EFE files. The editor shows it as on the EPS: each image is a folder with its directories \, the EFE files lie at the top. preset N \, presetstep and program changes go through all instruments \, in the order of the file names and the directories. An instrument is read in the background: notes go on sounding until it is in. \; Saving keeps the Ensoniq format: into an image the file goes as the EPS writes it (checked against the original operating system: it lists and loads what eps~ saved) \, at the top level as an EFE. So your library can go back onto the SD card of the ZuluSCSI as it is. A directory holds 38 files \, names have 12 characters. \; Before eps~ writes into an image it checks it: the free block count must match the FAT and every directory its file count \, otherwise it refuses and changes nothing. Every block it changes is first copied to <image>.undo beside the image: build/eps_fs_tool undo <image> puts the image back as it was before the first change (and deletes the journal). Delete the .undo file once you are happy \, and keep a copy of your SD card anyway. \; There is one library in Pd \, not one per object: two eps.i~ in one patch share it. Save the patch first \, an unsaved patch has no folder of its own. \; The controls of eps~ are offsets over the instrument while you play. Saving writes transpose \, tune \, cutoff \, filter 2 \, filter env \, attack \, decay and release into the instrument (into every wavesample) and sets them back to 0. vibrato \, wave position \, bend range \, patch select and vibrato rate are playing controls \, the EPS has no place for them in an instrument: they stay. volume and voices belong to the instrument object., f 64;
#X obj 60 4330 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Sampling 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4358 As on the EPS (SAMPLE \, Musician's Manual section 5): the audio in becomes a wavesample of the instrument that plays. eps.i~ takes Pd's audio input (input in the SAMPLE band \, 1 by default) plus its inlet 2 \, eps~ its inlet 4. Pd's audio must be on (DSP) with an input device chosen in the audio settings \, on a Mac Pd needs the permission for the microphone (System Settings \, Privacy). level shows whether anything comes in. There is no waveform display: set the points in the WS POINTS row afterwards \, by ear. \; Choose the rate (the seven of the EPS-16 PLUS \, 44.6 to 11.2 kHz: lower rates hold longer sounds \, they are band-limited as by the EPS's input filter) and where the recording goes: new WS (a new wavesample in the layer selected in the SELECT band) \, replace WS (the selected wavesample: its keys and parameters stay \, its loop too if it fits) \, new layer (up to 8) \, new instrument (UNNAMED INST \, as the EPS makes it). The recording uses the free sample memory of the EPS-16 PLUS (1024K words with the instrument): recinfo shows the seconds left. \; level shows the input as bars \, the star is the threshold. threshold 0 records at once on rec \, 1 to 19 (-54 to 0 dB in steps of 3) waits until the input crosses it \, pre ms keeps that much from before (10 to 20 ms are usually right). stop ends the recording (full memory too) \, then the editor says PLAY ROOT KEY: the next key you play is the key at which the recording plays back as recorded \, it does not sound. Then PLAY LOW KEY and PLAY HIGH KEY: the next two keys set the range of the new wavesample \, a Launchkey pad (or rec learn 0) keeps the keys it got. \; Key mapping as on the EPS: a new wavesample gets the keys between its root key and the root keys of its neighbours in the layer \, split at the midpoints (the whole keyboard when it is the first). Change it with root key \, low key and high key (the next key played sets it for the selected wavesample) or the cells WS key low / high: keys it gives up go to its neighbour. \; The recording is in the instrument that plays \, not yet on disk: save it with replace \, save copy or save as (a new instrument with save as or save copy). The file is the EPS's own: the original operating system loads and plays what eps~ recorded., f 64;
#X obj 60 5028 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Wavesample\ commands 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5056 The commands of the EPS's COMMAND/Wave \, LFO and Amp pages (Musician's Manual section 6) for the wavesample selected in the SELECT band. After do the result plays at once \, as KEEP=OLD NEW on the EPS: old and new switch between before and after \, keep takes the new one \, cancel the old one. Editing \, loading \, saving or the next command keep what plays. The algorithms follow the manual's descriptions \, the results are alike \, not the same bits. \; truncate: cuts the data before sample start and after sample end (not for a wavesample with copies \, as on the EPS). crossfade: the end of the loop fades into the data before loop start (zone: % of the loop \, depth: 3 dB smooth to 6 dB linear). reverse_xfade: into the data after loop start \, backwards. ensemble_xfade: the whole loop. bowtie_xfade: around both loop points \, zone up to 50 % \, needs data after loop end. The messages INCREMENT LOOPSTART and DECREMENT LOOPEND say there is not enough data before or after the loop. convert_rate: to one of the seven rates \, the pitch stays \, all points move. \; normalize: the whole data to full level. fade_in \, fade_out \, scale_data (from scale % start to end \, the depth curve) \, reverse_data \, invert_data \, clear_data \, volume_smooth (evens out the level \, smooth from very fine to very coarse \, at least 256 samples): over the range. Data commands change the copies that share the data. \; new_ws: a small square wave on the keys around C4 in the selected layer. copy_ws: a copy into copy to layer on the keys the original has (params only: it plays the same data \, with data: its own). delete_ws: not if copies use its data. \; new_layer: a new layer (up to 8) with a small square wave on all keys \, in patch 00. copy_layer: the selected layer into a new one \, its wavesamples as copies (with data: their own) \, in the same patches. delete_layer: the selected layer and its wavesamples \, not the last layer and not if another layer plays copies of them \, the patches follow. copy_params: all parameters of the selected wavesample to WS n (to WS in the editor \, encoder 8 on the Launchkey) \, not its data \, points \, loop mode \, root key \, tuning \, rate and keys. All of them can be heard with old / new before keep. \; These follow the descriptions in the EPS-16 PLUS External Command Specification (not measured in the OS): bidir_xfade makes both loop ends symmetric over the fade zone (at most 50 % of the loop) for a loop that plays forward and back. loop_longer (Make Loop Longer): after the loop comes the loop reversed \, the faded-out end and the faded-in reversed copy overlap over the fade zone \, the loop becomes twice as long less the zone. synth_loop: the loop made again from its spectrum with random phases \, smooth 0 to 4 smooths the spectrum (at most 65536 samples). \; copy_data / add_data: the range of the selected wavesample written over / added to WS n from its sample start (to WS \, add with clip prevention: the sum scaled to fit). replicate_data: the range repeated after itself up to the end of the data. mix (Mix Wavesamples): the selected one \, the source \, mixed into WS n \, balance -127 all source \, 0 half each \, 127 all destination. merge: the source \, then WS n \, crossfaded over the fade zone (% of the shorter one \, before the loop of WS n) \, into WS n \, balance -127 to 127 turns the destination or the source down. splice: the same without a fade. mix \, merge and splice need the same rate \, root key and tuning (else PITCH DIFFERENCE). \; alf (row MORE \, E5 ALF on the Launchkey): AUTO-LOOP FINDING as on the EPS \, on by default. A moved loop start or end goes to the place nearby where the loop joins best., f 64;
#X obj 60 6078 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 6106 name v: set a control \, see Controls. \; name: report it as info. \; n name v: set it from a pot or a MIDI CC \, 0 to 127. \; ninfo name: report it as info. \; cycle name [-1]: the next (previous) value \, round and round. \; dump: every control as info. \; e name v: set an instrument parameter (see Instrument \;   rows) from 0 to 127. einfo name: report it as info. \; edump: the selection (sel) and every instrument parameter. \; sel layer N \, sel ws N \, sel env N (1-3): select what the \;   LAYER \, WS and ENV rows edit\; sel layerstep / wsstep +-1. \;   ws N counts within the layer (WS 1..n of it \, as on the EPS). \;   Answers sel <layer> <ws> <env> <layers> <layer name> \;   <ws name> <info> <wavesamples in the layer>. \; follow 0/1: a played key selects its layer and wavesample. \; zerox 0/1: points snap to zero crossings. \; library [dir]: use this folder as the library and read \;   its list. Without dir: eps beside the external. \; libset <dir>: the library folder (relative to the patch's \;   folder or ~/...) \, kept in eps-library.txt beside the patch. \; libhome <dir> \, libarg <dir>: from eps.i~ at load (the folder \;   eps beside the patch \, argument 3). Answer: libdir <dir>. \; rescan: read the library folder again. \; preset n: load library instrument n (from 0) \, controls \;   back to 0. \; presetstep 1 or -1: the next or previous instrument. \; open file [k]: load instrument k (from 0) of any file \, \;   without the library. A name without a path is beside \;   the external. \; presets: list the library as preset n name. \; browse: report the folder shown (folder \, bsel). \; bstep 1 or -1 \, bselect k: move the selection in the folder. \; benter: enter the selected directory or load the selected \;   instrument. bup: the folder above. \; userstep 1 or -1: the next or previous instrument in the \;   folder of the one playing. \; nav step 1 or -1: the next or previous entry of the folder \;   shown (an instrument loads \, a folder is only shown). nav \;   open: into the folder shown. nav up: one level up (the \;   Launchkey pads > < OPEN EXIT). \; fxmode off / inst / bank / rom n / step 1 or -1: the effect \;   as on the EPS's EFFECT/Select page: OFF dry \, INST the \;   instrument's \, BANK the bank effect \, ROM 1-13 (global \, not \;   saved). Outlet: fxmode OFF|INST|BANK|ROM_n name. \; fx 0 or 1: FX=OFF \, or the mode before. fx: the effect and \;   its parameters (outlet: effect name rate count \, then \;   fxparam k name lo hi value item for each). \; fxparam k value: parameter k of the effect. \; fxpage 1 / -1 / 0: the next / previous / first page of eight \;   effect parameters \, the variation first (outlet: fxpage \;   effect page/pages variation on \, then fxcell k name 0-127 \;   value \, k 0-7). fxcell k 0-127: parameter k of the page. \; fxvar 1 / -1: the next / previous variation (round). \;   Editing a ROM effect makes it the bank effect (as the EPS). \; fxlist: the effect files (fxsource k name: EFE type 24 in \;   the library or a folder in it \, and in the images) and the \;   ROM effects (fxrom n name). fxsel 1 / -1: browse the files \;   (outlet fxpick name k/n) \, fxsel cancel. fxload [k]: the \;   file into the bank effect (LOAD EFFECT) \, FX=BANK. \; fxcopy bank: COPY CURRENT EFFECT TO BANK (what plays). \; fxcopy inst: the bank effect into the instrument (saved \;   with it). fxsave [name]: SAVE BANK EFFECT as an effect \;   file into the folder shown (a number added if taken). \; fxdelete: DELETE INST EFFECT \, the instrument keeps none. \; delete: delete the entry selected in the folder shown (an \;   instrument \, an empty folder \, an EFE file). \; init: every control back to 0 \, the instrument stays. \; reload: the instrument again \, edits dropped. \; saveas name: write the instrument as a new file into the \;   folder shown: into the image \, or name.efe at the top. \;   Refused if the name is there. \; replace: write it over the file it was loaded from. \; save: saveas with a free name \, the instrument's and a \;   number (the pads' save). \; mkdir name: a new directory in the folder shown (images). \; SysEx with a real EPS-16 PLUS (MIDI both ways \, SYS-EX ON in \;   its EDIT / System-MIDI page): \; epsch n: the EPS's MIDI base channel \, 1-16 (default 1). \; fetch i: instrument i (1-8) from the EPS's memory into the \;   folder shown as a new file \, then loaded. The effect does \;   not come along (SysEx cannot carry it). \; fetchws i l w: wavesample w of layer l as name.wav into the \;   library folder. \; send i: the instrument that plays into the EPS's empty \;   instrument i (1-8\; delete it there first). Copies share \;   their data as in the file. The effect stays the EPS's. \; sendws i l w file.wav: the WAV (library folder) into \;   wavesample w of layer l \, which must exist. One that has \;   copies keeps its old length (the EPS will not cut it). \; sxcancel: stop a transfer. Outlet 3: sysex step percent \, \;   fetched \, sent. \;   All three write the offsets into the instrument first. \; The wave recorder (see Sampling): \; rec rate n (0-6: 44.6 29.8 22.3 17.9 14.9 12.8 11.2 kHz) \, \;   rec ratestep 1 or -1. \; rec thresh n: 0 (record at once) to 19 (-54 to 0 dB). \; rec pre ms: pre-trigger \, 0 to 127 ms (default 15). \; rec dest n: 0 a new wavesample in the selected layer \, 1 \;   replace the selected wavesample \, 2 a new layer \, 3 a new \;   instrument. \; rec level 0/1: the level display (recmeter) without \;   recording. \; rec start: record (from the threshold). rec stop: stop \, then \;   the next key is the root key. Stop again: cancel. \; rec root n: the root key without playing it. \; rec learn root / lo / hi: the next key played sets the root \;   key / lowest / highest key of the selected wavesample. \; rec monitor 0/1: hear the input (on / off \, always). \; lkgfx 0/1: the Launchkey pictures off / on (default on). \; env copy / env paste: the selected envelope of the selected \;   wavesample into a buffer / from it (E16 COPY and PSTE). \; lk 0/1: the Launchkey surface off / on (eps.i~: on). \; lk edit [0/1] \, lk mode: EDIT / PLAY. lk page <P1 .. E20>. \; lk legend: show the pads. lk sync: colours and values again. \; lk pad <note> <velocity> \, lk cc <cc> <value>: as from the \;   Launchkey. padchannel n: the pads' channel (default 10). \; lk status: answers lk <play|edit> <page> <on>\; lkscreen \;   <small> <line 1> <line 2>: what the display shows. \; rec input n: eps.i~ records Pd's audio input 0 none \, 1 in 1 \;   (default) \, 2 in 2 \, 3 both \, inlet 2 always. \; rec status: report the recorder's settings. \; The wavesample commands (see Wavesample commands): \; cmd name or cmd n: choose one (truncate crossfade \;   reverse_xfade ensemble_xfade bowtie_xfade convert_rate \;   normalize fade_in fade_out volume_smooth scale_data \;   reverse_data invert_data clear_data new_ws copy_ws \;   delete_ws new_layer copy_layer delete_layer copy_params \;   bidir_xfade loop_longer synth_loop copy_data add_data \;   replicate_data mix merge splice) \, \;   cmd step 1 or -1. \; cmd range n: 0 sample \, 1 loop \, 2 start to loop \, 3 loop to end. \; cmd depth n (0-5: 3.0 3.5 4.0 4.5 5.5 6.0 dB) \, cmd zone % \, \;   cmd sstart % \, cmd send % (scale data \, 0-200) \, cmd rate n \;   (0-6 \, convert) \, cmd smooth n (0-4) \, cmd layer n \, cmd data \;   0/1 (copy with its data) \, cmd ws n (copy_params: to WS n). \; cmd do: run it on the selected wavesample. cmd old \, cmd new: \;   hear before and after. cmd keep \, cmd cancel: decide. \; cmd status: report the settings. \; bend f: pitch wheel \, -1 to 1 \, times bend. \; mod f: modulation wheel \, 0 to 1 (EPS source WHEEL). \; pressure f: channel pressure \, 0 to 1 (PRESS). \; polypressure note f: pressure of one key (PRESS). \; pedal f \, xctrl f: the sources PEDAL and XCTRL \, 0 to 1. \; sustain 0/1: hold pedal. \; channel n: MIDI receive channel \, 0 is all. \; inst k: select location k (1-8) \, inst: all (outlet inst k \;   name channel \, instsel k \, instcur name channel). inststep \;   1 / -1. instch k ch: the channel of location k (0: only \;   selected) \, instch ch: of the selected. instdelete [k]: \;   DELETE INSTRUMENT (default the selected). \; banksave [name]: SAVE BANK into the folder shown of an \;   image: the locations (their files on that disk \, a copy \;   when two hold the same) \, volumes \, the bank effect. \;   bankdevice n: the device written (0 floppy \, 1-8 SCSI \;   0-7 \, -1 as loaded or guessed). A bank (type 23 \, in an \;   image or an EFE at the top) loads with benter / nav \;   open (outlet bank name). \; txchannel n: channel of the controller feedback \, 1 to 16. \; thru 0/1: MIDI thru \, on by default. \; status: report instrument \, channels \, library size and \;   sounding voices. \; stop \, reset: all notes off., f 64;
#X obj 60 8712 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty The\ instrument 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 8740 eps~ reads the instruments of the Ensoniq EPS \, EPS-16 PLUS and ASR-10 from their own files: layers \, wavesamples with their samples \, loops and loop modes \, envelopes \, filters \, pan \, patch select and the wave modulation (transwave). It plays them on a model of the ES5505 voice chip of the EPS-16 PLUS \, taken from MAME: interpolation \, the 4-pole filter in its four arrangements \, the 8-bit logarithmic volume \, forward \, backward and bidirectional loops \, the 2/1024 pitch steps. \; What the EPS operating system does is rebuilt on top: voice allocation \, layers and patch select \, the three envelopes (pitch \, filter \, amp) with the two-stage release \, attack velocity \, keyboard time scaling and the finite mode \, the LFO with its seven waves \, delay \, reset and humanize \, random pitch \, the modulation of pitch \, both filters \, amp and pan from the 15 sources (LFO \, RANDM \, ENV1 \, ENV2 \, PR+VL \, VEL \, VEL1 \, VEL2 \, KBD \, PITCH \, WHEEL \, PEDAL \, XCTRL \, PRESS \, WL+PR \, numbered as in the External Command Specification) \, crossfades \, layer glide and all seven wave modulation types (loop position \, sample start \, both \, loop start \, loop end \, loop start-X \, transwave). \; Calibrated against the original operating system (OS 1.30 in an emulator \, register traces of test instruments): cutoff scale of both filters \, volume and envelope level law \, pan law \, boost \, envelope times and shapes \, release \, LFO speeds and depth \, wave modulation types and range \, the pitch \, filter and key amounts \, the mod sources 0-11. Still approximations: the soft/hard velocity levels \, amp and pan modulation amounts \, crossfade curves \, glide (every mode is mono with glide). Not there: pitch tables. The controls of eps~ are offsets over the instrument \, 0 plays it as stored. \; Effects: the instrument's effect runs as on the EPS-16 PLUS \, with the ROM and OS of your EPS: put the two ROM dumps (U27 lower \, U28 upper \, 64 KB each \, names ending .u27 / .u28 \, or both chips as one file eps16plus-rom.bin) and the OS 1.30 file (eps16plus-os.efe or the OS EFE as it is) into the library. A 68000 runs the effect's own driver code with the helpers of ROM and OS and an ES5510 (ESP) the effect program at the effect's rate (29.8 \, 44.6 or 78.1 kHz). The wavesamples go to the effect by their output bus \, bus 3 (aux) stays dry. Without the two files eps~ plays dry. Mod sources of the effect: bend \, wheel \, xctrl \, pedal \, sustain \, pressure. The effects work as on the EPS: FX=INST plays the instrument's effect (saved with it) \, FX=BANK the bank effect (effect files load into it \, SAVE BANK EFFECT writes it as a file) \, FX=ROM 1-13 the effects of the ROM \, global and not saved: HALL REVERB \, 44KHZ REVERB \, ROOM REVERB \, DUAL DELAYS \, 44KHZ DELAYS \, CHORUS+REVERB \, PHASER+REVERB \, FLANGER+REV \, ROT. SPKR+REV \, CHOR+REV+DDL \, CMP+DIST+REV \, DIST+CHO+REV \, WAH+DIST+REV. A ROM effect edited becomes the bank effect. COPY CURRENT EFFECT copies what plays into the bank \, or the bank effect into the instrument. FX mix (P2 \, encoder 5) blends the effect towards the voices without it: 127 as stored \, 0 no effect. \; The output runs at Pd's sample rate \, not at the 29.76 kHz of the EPS-16 PLUS. Up to 32 voices \, 20 by default., f 64;
#X obj 60 9602 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Data\ files 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 9630 Building needs no data. To play \, put Ensoniq instruments into the folder eps beside your patch: single files (.efe from EpsLin \, EnDiskEx or Chicken Translator) or whole disk images (.img from a floppy \, an SD card of a ZuluSCSI or BlueSCSI \, .ede and .eda from Giebler's tools \, .gkh). HFE floppy images are converted to IMG first. The EPS \, the EPS-16 PLUS and the ASR-10 share the format \, tested so far with EPS-16 PLUS instruments. \; For eps.i~ two files are enough: eps~ (the external) and eps.i~.pd in a folder on Pd's search path., f 64;
#X obj 60 9804 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 9832 In the order of the editor: one heading per row \, the same title as the row there \, page k on the controller is row k. Each line: name (the label in the editor) \, range \, CC number and what it does. Page 1 is P1 PERFORM of the Launchkey: the two filters \, the filter envelope and the amp envelope. Page 2 is P2 PLAY: volume \, transpose \, wave position \, filter envelope. The row MORE has no CC: the editor and the pads (patch select)., f 64;
#X obj 60 9974 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 1\ \ PERFORM\ \ CC\ 20\ 21\ 22\ 23\ 24\ 25\ 26\ 27 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 10002 cut (Cutoff) -63..63 \, CC 20: cutoff of filter 1 of every \;   wavesample \, also of sounding notes. 0 leaves the instrument \;   as it is \; cut2 (Filter 2) -63..63 \, CC 21: cutoff of filter 2 (the second \;   low-pass \, or the high-pass in the modes with one) \, also of \;   sounding notes. The EPS has no resonance \, this takes its \;   place on page 1 \; fatt (F attack) -63..63 \, CC 22: attack of the filter envelope \;   (ENV2): time 1 \, for the notes that follow \; fdec (F decay) -63..63 \, CC 23: decay of the filter envelope: \;   times 2 to 4 \, for the notes that follow \; frel (F release) -63..63 \, CC 24: release of the filter \;   envelope: times 5 and 6 \, also for notes already held \; att (Attack) -63..63 \, CC 25: attack: time 1 of the amp \;   envelope \, in steps of the panel's 0-99 times \, for the notes \;   that follow \; dec (Decay) -63..63 \, CC 26: decay: times 2 to 4 of the amp \;   envelope \, for the notes that follow \; rel (Release) -63..63 \, CC 27: release: times 5 and 6 of the \;   amp envelope \, also for notes already held, f 64;
#X obj 60 10336 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 2\ \ PLAY\ \ CC\ 28\ 29\ 30\ 31\ 33 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 10364 volume (Volume) 0..127 \, CC 28: master volume \, 100 = unity \, not \;   stored \; transpose (Transpose) -24..24 \, CC 29: transposition in \;   semitones \, of the keyboard and the pitch \; wave (Wave pos) 0..127 \, CC 30: position of the wave modulation \;   (transwave \, loop position): added to the wavesample's mod \;   source \, as if the wheel were turned up. No effect on \;   wavesamples without wave modulation \; fenv (Filter env) -63..63 \, CC 31: added to the filter envelope \;   amount of every wavesample \, also of sounding notes \; fxmix (FX mix) 0..127 \, CC 33: the effect against the voices \;   without it: 127 = as the instrument has it \, 0 = no effect \;   (the effect keeps running \, its tail fades with the mix), f 64;
#X obj 60 10586 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MORE\ \ no\ CC\ (editor\ and\ pads)\ \ no\ CC\ (mouse\ only) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 10614 patch (Patch sel) 0..3: patch select: which layers play \, as \;   the two patch buttons of the EPS \; tune (Tune) -50..50: fine tuning in cents \; bend (Bend range) 0..12: bender range in semitones \; vib (Vibrato) 0..127: vibrato of eps~ itself (not the \;   instrument's LFO) \, up to a semitone \; vibrate (Vib rate) 0..127: rate of the vibrato \, 0.1 to 12 Hz \; voices (Voices) 1..32: polyphony: 20 as on the EPS-16 PLUS \, up \;   to the 32 of the ES5505 \, not stored \; xcc (XCTRL CC) 0..119: the MIDI controller that is the XCTRL \;   mod source (2 = breath \, as on the EPS) \, not stored \; alf (Auto loop) 0..1: AUTO-LOOP FINDING as on the EPS: a moved \;   loop point goes where the loop joins best (on), f 64;
#X obj 60 10836 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Instrument\ rows 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 10864 The rows below the controls edit the instrument (mouse only \, message e). Each line: name (label) and range of the value as stored \, what it is., f 64;
#X obj 60 10926 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty INSTRUMENT 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 10954 i_trans (Transpose) -36..36: transposition of the instrument \;   in semitones \; i_keylo (Key low) 21..108: lowest key the instrument plays \; i_keyhi (Key high) 21..108: highest key the instrument plays \; i_press (Pressure) 0..3: pressure mode as stored (0..3) \; i_psel (Patch mode) 0..4: patch select mode: LIVE and HELD \;   start in patch 00 \, 0* *0 ** start in that patch (measured in \;   the OS: the patch the instrument plays after loading) \; i_prog (MIDI prog) 0..127: MIDI program as stored \; i_mout (MIDI out ch) 0..16: MIDI out channel as stored, f 64;
#X obj 60 11128 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty LAYER 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 11156 l_vello (Vel low) 0..127: lowest velocity the layer plays \; l_velhi (Vel high) 0..127: highest velocity the layer plays \; l_glmode (Glide mode) 0..5: glide mode as stored (eps~: any \;   mode is mono with glide) \; l_gltime (Glide time) 0..99: glide time \; l_delay (Delay) 0..99: delay before the layer sounds \; l_dlyvel (Delay vel) -127..127: velocity modulation of the \;   delay \; l_restrk (Restrike) 0..99: restrike decay \; l_legato (Legato) 0..1: legato layer, f 64;
#X obj 60 11330 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty LAYER\ PATCHES 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 11358 l_in00 (In 00) 0..1: the layer plays in patch 00 \; l_in0x (In 0*) 0..1: the layer plays in patch 0* \; l_inx0 (In *0) 0..1: the layer plays in patch *0 \; l_inxx (In **) 0..1: the layer plays in patch ** \; l_keyup (Key up) 0..1: the layer sounds on key up \; l_stlink (Stereo link) 0..1: stereo link \; l_ptable (Pitch table) 0..1: pitch table (not played by eps~), f 64;
#X obj 60 11484 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty WS\ POINTS 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 11512 w_sst (Smp start) 0..127: sample start \, coarse \; w_sstf (fine) 0..127: sample start \, fine \; w_send (Smp end) 0..127: sample end \, coarse \; w_sendf (fine) 0..127: sample end \, fine \; w_lst (Loop start) 0..127: loop start \, coarse \; w_lstf (fine) 0..127: loop start \, fine \; w_lend (Loop end) 0..127: loop end \, coarse \; w_lendf (fine) 0..127: loop end \, fine, f 64;
#X obj 60 11654 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty WS\ LOOP\ /\ KEYS 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 11682 w_loop (Loop mode) 0..4: loop mode \; w_lpos (Loop pos) 0..127: loop position: moves loop start and \;   end together \, coarse \; w_lposf (fine) 0..127: loop position \, fine \; w_keylo (WS key low) 21..108: lowest key of the wavesample in \;   the layer \; w_keyhi (WS key high) 21..108: highest key of the wavesample \;   in the layer, f 64;
#X obj 60 11824 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty WS\ PITCH 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 11852 w_root (Root key) 21..108: root key \; w_fine (Fine) -127..127: fine tune \, 1/128 semitone \; w_bend (Bend range) 0..13: bender range in semitones \, 13 = \;   global \; w_penv (ENV1 pitch) -127..127: pitch envelope amount \; w_plfo (LFO pitch) -127..127: LFO to pitch \; w_psrc (Pitch mod) 0..15: pitch modulation source \; w_pamt (Pitch amt) -127..127: pitch modulation amount \; w_rand (Random) 0..127: random pitch amount, f 64;
#X obj 60 12010 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty WS\ FILTER\ 1 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 12038 w_fmode (Filt mode) 0..3: filter mode as on the EPS: F1 poles \;   low pass / F2 poles low or high pass (2LP/2HP \, 3LP/1HP \, \;   2LP/2LP \, 3LP/1LP) \; w_cut1 (Cutoff 1) 0..150: cutoff of filter 1 \; w_key1 (Key 1) -127..127: key tracking of filter 1 \; w_env1 (Env 1) -127..127: ENV2 amount on filter 1 \; w_fsrc1 (Mod 1) 0..15: modulation source of filter 1 \; w_famt1 (Mod amt 1) -127..127: modulation amount of filter 1, f 64;
#X obj 60 12180 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty WS\ FILTER\ 2 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
